kosha matra-aayaama

  -- matra-aayaama: SI dimension exponent vectors for all units.
  -- each unit maps to [M, L, T, I, theta, N, J, scale].
  -- the exponent vector IS the unit's identity.
  -- kramanusara (d/dt) subtracts 1 from the T exponent.
  -- the T exponent depth = kramanusara depth.

  "physics-varga-vishesa"
  "matra-sthita kramanusara-yukta"
  "yantra-sthita aayaama-yukta"


done
